{% extends 'AdminInterfaceBundle:Layout:list.html.twig' %}
{% block listpane_content %}
	<section class="dp-paneblock dp-listpane">
		<header>
			<nav>
				<span class="status-pinger saved-ping" dp-ping-flash="display_orders">
					<i class="fa fa-check-square-o-square"></i>
					{{ phrase('agent.general.saved') }}
				</span>

				{% include 'AdminInterfaceBundle:Layout:standard-settings-menu.html.twig' %}
			</nav>
			<h3 ng-pluralize count="ListCtrl.deps.length || 0"
				when="{{ ng_plural_phrase('adm.general.x_departments') }}"></h3>
		</header>
		<article>
			<ul class="dp-item-list" ui-sortable="ListCtrl.sortedListOptions" dp-list-autoload dp-max-height>
				<li class="with-drag-handle" ng-repeat="dep in ListCtrl.depList"
					dp-state-mark="chat.chat_deps.edit.{{ ng_var('dep.id') }}" data-id="{{ ng_var('dep.id') }}">

					<a href="{{ ng_href('chat.chat_deps.edit', '{id: dep.id}') }}">
						<i class="fa fa-bars drag-handle"></i>
						<h4><span class="title-id" title="ID">#{{ ng_var('dep.id') }}</span> <span class="title-text">{{ ng_var('dep.title') }}</span></h4>
					</a>

					<ul class="dp-item-list sublist" ng-show="dep.children.length"
						ui-sortable="ListCtrl.sortedListOptions">
						<li class="with-drag-handle" ng-repeat="subdep in dep.children"
							dp-state-mark="chat.chat_deps.edit.{{ ng_var('subdep.id') }}"
							data-id="{{ ng_var('subdep.id') }}">
							<a href="{{ ng_href('chat.chat_deps.edit', '{id: subdep.id}') }}">
								<i class="fa fa-bars drag-handle"></i>
								<h4>
									<span class="tree-char middle" ng-if="!$last"></span>
									<span class="tree-char last" ng-if="$last"></span>
									<span class="title-id" title="ID">#{{ ng_var('subdep.id') }}</span>
									<span class="title-text">{{ ng_var('subdep.title') }}</span>
								</h4>
							</a>
						</li>
					</ul>

				</li>
			</ul>
			<div class="dp-add-control">
				<a class="btn btn-default" ng-class="{'active': isStateActive('.create') }"
				   href="{{ ng_href('chat.chat_deps.gocreate') }}" dp-list-autoload autoload-priority="2">
					<i class="fa fa-plus"></i> New Department
				</a>
			</div>

			<div class="dp-empty-list-notice" ng-show="ListCtrl.deps.length == 1">
				<p>
					{{ phrase('adm.departments.not_user_visible') }}
				</p>
			</div>
		</article>
	</section>

	<div dp-register-message="no_delete_last">{{ phrase('adm.departments.no_delete_last') }}</div>
{% endblock %}
{% block listpane_help %}
	<header>
		<h1>Departments are a way to divide up the helpdesk and control access.</h1>
		<p>You can use departments to limit agent and user access. Chat departments are separate from ticket departments.</p>
	</header>

	<article>
		<section>
			<p>
				Here are some important features of chat departments:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Agent chat permissions are based upon departments; you can create agents that can view some chats but not others.</li>
				<li>User chat permissions are based upon departments; you can set a usergroup so that members can open chats in some departments but not others.</li>
				<li>You can set a user-facing department name to be displayed only to users e.g. agents see "Terms of Service Violations", while users see "Support".</li>
				<li>Each chat will always have a department.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span>FAQ</span></h2>
			<dl>
				<dt><em>Q:</em> How many departments can I have?</dt>
				<dd><em>A:</em> You can have an unlimited number of departments. Typically, companies will have less than ten departments, but you can structure your departments as you feel suitable.</dd>

				<dt><em>Q:</em> Can I use sub-departments/child departments?</dt>
				<dd><em>A:</em>
					Yes. A department can have sub-departments,
					e.g. the "Support" department can contain "Support Tier 1" and "Support Tier 2".<br/>
					Note that you can't assign tickets to a department if it contains sub-departments;
					you must assign to the sub-departments. In the example above, you could assign chats to "Support Tier 1" and "Support Tier 2",
					but not to "Support".
				</dd>

				<dt><em>Q:</em> I don't need departments - can I disable the field?</dt>
				<dd><em>A:</em>
					Chats always have a department, but if you only have one department defined,
					it will not be shown to users, effectively disabling the field.
				</dd>

				<dt><em>Q:</em> What is the difference between ticket departments and chat departments?</dt>
				<dd><em>A:</em>
					Like chat departments, ticket departments are the key field for grouping chats.
					The two types of departments are not linked together - you can have different departments for tickets and chats.
				</dd>

				<dt><em>Q:</em>My helpdesk uses multiple languages and some of the department names are not being translated; how do I fix this?</dt>
				<dd><em>A:</em>
					You need to enter a translation for the department names. Go to <strong>Setup > Languages</strong>; click on each language you have installed beyond the default, click <strong>Edit Phrases</strong>, and enter a custom translation.
				</dd>
			</dl>
		</section>
		<section class="related-content">
			<h2><span>Related Content</span></h2>
			<ul>
				<li><i class="fa fa-book"></i> <a href="https://www.deskpro.com/manuals/admin-manual/admin-manual.html#chat" target="_blank">Chat</a></li>
			</ul>
	</section>
	</article>
{% endblock %}
